{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>במלאת שפקו</b> — When he reaches all that suffices him, then it is distressing to him, and the hand of the laborers comes upon him, like the matter of 'בפרוח רשעים' (in the flowering of the wicked). And some say: when the day of their downfall arrives. And like it: 'תחת רשעים ספקם' (Job 21:16). Like 'ויספק את כפיו הכה' (he struck, he clapped his hands)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The second comparison (תחת רשעים ספקם) cites Job 21:16; 'וספק את כפיו הכה' paraphrases 2 Kings 5:27 (Leprosy of Gehazi), where the root ספק denotes striking."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:16.060026647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}